# Domain enums

Place each enum in its own `Enums/<Name>.cs` under Domain. Use a file-scoped namespace ending in `.Domain.Enums` and PascalCase names.
Assign each member an explicit integer. For a new sequence, start at zero with the appropriate initial value. Preserve assigned numbers when a stored or published enum evolves.
Use three-line Russian summaries on the type and each member. Separate members with a blank line and keep the trailing comma.

```csharp
namespace Catalog.Domain.Enums;

/// <summary>
/// Состояние каталога.
/// </summary>
public enum CatalogState
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Подготовка к публикации.
    /// </summary>
    Draft = 0,

    /// <summary>
    /// Каталог опубликован.
    /// </summary>
    Published = 1,
}
```
